# ============================================================================
#  CTN 2026 — .gitignore
# ============================================================================
#  Two competition rules drive the contents of this file. Do not remove
#  entries without reading them.
#
#  Rule 5.6  Never share competition API keys or credentials beyond your team.
#            -> Hardcoding a key and pushing is itself a breach; deleting it
#               afterwards does not help, because it stays in git history.
#            -> If a key leaks, rotate it immediately and notify the organisers.
#
#  Rule 5.2  Do not leak competition materials (rules PDFs, participant
#            briefings, Discord screenshots, ...) beyond your team.
#
#  Also: this repository MUST stay **private** for the duration of the
#  competition. Publishing your code hands your strategy to the other teams
#  (especially since prompt injection against other agents is permitted).
#  If you open-source it afterwards (allowed by Rule 10.4), first confirm that
#  none of the categories below ever entered the history.
# ============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Secrets and credentials  <- highest priority (Rule 5.6)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# Keep the value-free template only (variable names present, values absent).
# NOTE: the comment must be on its own line. A trailing `#` in a .gitignore
#       pattern is NOT a comment — it becomes part of the pattern and the
#       negation below silently stops matching.
!.env.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

secrets/
credentials/
credentials*.json
service-account*.json
*_token.txt
*_secret*


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Runtime state  <- never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Rationale: state changes every second (huge, meaningless diffs), it is
#  large, and `git pull` into a directory that holds live state files causes
#  conflicts — which stops the fleet mid-run while the competition is live.
#  State needs *backups*, not *version control*.
state/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
checkpoint*
*.ckpt


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Telemetry and logs  <- never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Rationale: large, and contains platform content plus telemetry data
#  (Rules 4.3 / 6.4 cover data handling).
logs/
*.log
*.jsonl
!strategy/**/*.jsonl   # exception: hand-maintained strategy corpora may be tracked


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Competition materials  <- never committed (Rule 5.2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  For rules documents, participant sheets and official client templates:
#  confirm with the organisers before tracking anything they supplied.
materials/
briefings/
official/
*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx
*.xlsx
discord-export*
screenshots/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Conda / environments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The environment is defined by environment.yml + scripts/setup_env.sh and is
#  part of the repository. Locally created environment directories, exported
#  lock files and the conda cache are not.
.conda/
envs/
environment.lock.yml
*.conda.lock


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python

venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
pip-wheel-metadata/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
junit*.xml


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Local caches / scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*~
scratch/
playground/
*.local.*
local_*
# Local JEV task lists and decision notes (user requirement: never commit)
/JEV_TASKS.local.md
/JEV_INPUT_CONTRACT.local.md
# 中文决策树仅本地查看（用户要求：不上传 Git）
/jev-decision-tree-zh.html


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Editors / operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.sublime-*
.history/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Explicitly tracked  <- these MUST be committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Rule 7.5: finalist teams must submit all source code, scripts and tools
#  used during the competition. The following therefore **must** stay tracked;
#  never add them to any ignore rule:
#
#    ctn/**/*.py             source code
#    strategy/**             argument matrix, persona voice specs, Jev question
#                            set, thresholds
#                            (the corpus is part of the "source", and its git
#                            history IS the story you present in Sydney)
#    PREDICTIONS.md          pre-registered hypotheses (the calibration baseline)
#    requirements.txt        dependencies
#    Dockerfile              container image
#    deploy.sh               deployment script
#    systemd/*.service       process supervision
#    docs/**                 documentation
#    .env.example            configuration template (variable names only)
